{
  "notes": "tp4-trace.json with the device-side row trace on as well, mounting the overlay's three tap files too (attention, compressor, Engram; tp4-trace.json mounts the other four): on every rank, 64-bit digests of every row, for steps of at most 64 rows, of each target-forward tap in order: all-reduce and all-gather inputs and outputs, each compressor's projected values and emitted latents and its ratio-2 ring carry, each indexer's top-k selection, each attention layer's output before WO, and each Engram layer's gathered table rows and output; plus positions, token ids and final hidden states. Inside CUDA graphs. Costs roughly 200 taps a forward (three to six small kernels each, an estimated 15-20% of a c1 step) and one 400 KB device-to-host copy a step. For the first-divergence trace of the determinism gate. Not a candidate.",
